@startuml
title PeaPod - Menu (LCD + Rotary Encoder)

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
hide empty members

package "PeaPod::Menu" {
  enum PEAPOD_MENU_T {
    PEAPOD_MENU_MAIN = 0
    PEAPOD_MENU_MODULE = 1
    PEAPOD_MENU_DEVICE = 2
    PEAPOD_MENU_FLAG = 3
    PEAPOD_MENU_VARIABLE = 4
    PEAPOD_MENU_SET = 5
  }

  class peapod_menustate_t <<struct>> {
    +menu: PEAPOD_MENU_T
    +submenu: uint8_t
    +module_idx: uint8_t
  }

  object "menu_state" as MenuState <<State<peapod_menustate_t>>>

  object "Menu API" as MenuAPI {
    initializeDevices(): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    update(): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    --
    onEncoderChange(inc: bool)
    onEncoderPress()
    writeLCDMenu(menu: peapod_menustate_t)
    --
    fqa_lcd: i2cip_fqa_t (MCP23008, fake MUX)
    fqa_encoder: i2cip_fqa_t (Seesaw, fake MUX)
    errlev_lcd / errlev_encoder: i2cip_errorlevel_t
    lcd: LCD*
  }
}

class LCD

MenuState ..> peapod_menustate_t : wraps
MenuState ..> PEAPOD_MENU_T
MenuAPI ..> MenuState : encoder events set state
MenuState ..> MenuAPI : writeLCDMenu callback
MenuAPI ..> LCD : render

note right of MenuState
FSM::State specialized for the menu struct:
compare() always returns true, so every
set() unconditionally fires writeLCDMenu
(pure event-driven redraw).
end note

note bottom of MenuAPI
update() runs every loop iteration:
1) read Seesaw encoder (delta + button)
2) translate to onEncoderChange/onEncoderPress
3) menu_state.set(...) -> LCD redraw

Menu hierarchy: Main -> Module -> Device,
or Main -> Flag/Variable -> Set (edit value).
Both devices sit on the fake (direct-wire) MUX.
end note

@enduml
